The function was already minimal. This version reads `profile` and `profileIndex` into locals once, so the compiler can keep them in registers instead of reloading members. The null-check and bounds-check semantics are unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 Field::GetNumComponents(void) const
{
    const auto* const p = profile;
    if (p == NULL)
        return 0;
    const auto idx = profileIndex;
    if (idx >= p->numFields)
        return 0;
    return p->fields[idx].numComponents;
}
```